Third-party components vendored in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

vendor/llama.cpp/ — llama.cpp, the inference engine (pinned commit recorded in
    scripts/llamacpp-patches/UPSTREAM, built with the patches in that
    directory). Not linked into IdleToken binaries: llama-server and the
    ggml rpc-server are spawned as separate processes and are shipped inside
    the installers.
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
    MIT License — full text in vendor/llama.cpp/LICENSE
    Upstream: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

vendor/ds4/ — ds4.c, the DeepSeek V4 Flash single-machine reference engine.
    Compiled into and linked with both idletoken-worker and idletoken-coord
    (ds4.c, ds4_cuda.cu / ds4_metal.m); the Metal shader sources are also read
    at runtime. Not merely a reference.
    Copyright (c) 2026 The ds4.c authors
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
    MIT License — full text in vendor/ds4/LICENSE
    Upstream: https://github.com/antirez/ds4 (pinned commit in vendor/ds4/UPSTREAM)

vendor/ds4/rax.c, rax.h, rax_malloc.h — Rax, a radix tree implementation.
    Also linked into both binaries. It sits inside vendor/ds4/ but is NOT
    covered by that directory's MIT LICENSE, which is why it is listed
    separately: the BSD 3-clause terms require this notice in binary
    redistributions too.
    Copyright (c) 2017-2026, Salvatore Sanfilippo <antirez at gmail dot com>
    BSD 3-Clause — full text in the header of vendor/ds4/rax.c

vendor/tweetnacl/ — TweetNaCl, "a crypto library in 100 tweets"
    Public domain, dedicated by D. J. Bernstein, Bernard van Gastel,
    Wesley Janssen, Tanja Lange, Peter Schwabe, Sjaak Smetsers.
    Upstream: https://tweetnacl.cr.yp.to/20140427/

vendor/blake2/ — BLAKE2b (RFC 7693), unkeyed one-shot subset
    Public domain / CC0, matching the upstream reference dedication by
    Samuel Neves and Jean-Philippe Aumasson.
    Upstream: https://github.com/BLAKE2/BLAKE2

Model weights are NOT distributed with this software. IdleToken downloads
GGUF files published by their respective authors; those files carry their
own licenses (DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 is MIT, per its model card).

